1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,830
A shortcut: count the power of mole in the unit, and subtract it from one.

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:12,460
Litres per mole per second has mole to the minus one, so the order is one minus minus one, two.

3
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:19,257
And a first order k has no concentration in it at all, so it can be quoted per second, per minute or per year.

